(air whooshing)

267
00:17:57,702 --> 00:17:58,535
(hand thudding)

268
00:17:58,536 --> 00:18:01,747
(engine whistling)

269
00:18:01,748 --> 00:18:04,917
(footsteps plodding)

270
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:11,673
- Well, Sean, looks like
Elvis done left the building.

271
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:14,259
(Sean sighing)

272
00:18:17,764 --> 00:18:20,516
(engine humming)

273
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:25,270
[Jamie] It wasn't my fault.

274
00:18:25,271 --> 00:18:27,731
Why won't you ever be on my side?

275
00:18:27,732 --> 00:18:29,233
I am always on your side,

276
00:18:29,234 --> 00:18:31,109
but you have to give me a chance.

277
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,361
Now what?

278
00:18:32,362 --> 00:18:33,570
(Eve sighing)

279
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:35,072
She was suspended again.

280
00:18:35,073 --> 00:18:36,657
Some kid made a crack about her clothes.

281
00:18:36,658 --> 00:18:37,491
She started a fight.

282
00:18:37,492 --> 00:18:38,325
[Jamie] That's right, Dad.

283
00:18:38,326 --> 00:18:39,826
Don't even ask me what happened.

284
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:44,414
- Okay, what happened?
(pensive music)

285
00:18:48,419 --> 00:18:49,753
Oh, I see.

286
00:18:49,754 --> 00:18:50,712
(footsteps plodding)

287
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:52,631
Not like you would believe me anyway.

288
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:55,217
- Jamie, look, it, it,
it's not easy, okay?

289
00:18:55,218 --> 00:18:57,052
I mean, look. (sighs)

290
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:59,429
You change the way you look every week

291
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:01,265
and, and, and the way you act.

292
00:19:01,266 --> 00:19:04,184
Who are you supposed to be now?

293
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:06,603
I'm supposed to be me.

294
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:08,772
Not like you have a clue who I am anyway.

295
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:12,442
(footsteps plodding)

296
00:19:12,443 --> 00:19:13,402
(door clattering)

297
00:19:13,403 --> 00:19:15,988
(Sean sighing)

298
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:20,492
Uh, I have to work tonight.

299
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:22,786
I called to tell you, but I
was on hold for 10 minutes,

300
00:19:22,787 --> 00:19:24,413
and I couldn't wait any longer.

301
00:19:24,414 --> 00:19:25,914
I got him, Eve.

302
00:19:25,915 --> 00:19:28,584
(pensive music)

303
00:19:30,295 --> 00:19:31,295
It's over?

304
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,089
It's over.

305
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:39,303
Oh, Sean.

306
00:19:39,304 --> 00:19:42,431
(gentle music)

307
00:19:42,432 --> 00:19:44,308
I'll make it up to you and Jamie.

308
00:19:44,309 --> 00:19:45,142
I promise.

309
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:47,603
I'll put in for a desk job.

310
00:19:47,604 --> 00:19:51,023
We'll all, all do counseling,
sit down, talk about Mikey.

311
00:19:51,024 --> 00:19:53,150
I'll do it, anything you want.

312
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:54,234
(Eve exhales)

313
00:19:54,235 --> 00:19:56,695
[Eve] I just want you. (laughs)

314
00:19:56,696 --> 00:19:57,529
(laughing) Well, good,

315
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:58,780
'cause that's what you're gonna get.

316
00:19:58,781 --> 00:19:59,698
(Eve laughing)

317
00:19:59,699 --> 00:20:00,532
Happy?

318
00:20:01,451 --> 00:20:02,868
Uh, yes, yeah.

319
00:20:05,496 --> 00:20:08,915
(gentle music continues)

320
00:20:16,257 --> 00:20:19,092
(footsteps plodding)

321
00:20:19,093 --> 00:20:20,844
[Coworker] Hold up.

322
00:20:20,845 --> 00:20:24,014
(coworkers clapping)

323
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,524
What is all this?

324
00:20:36,569 --> 00:20:39,071
Sir, the CIA sent this over.

325
00:20:40,281 --> 00:20:41,865
I didn't know they catered.

326
00:20:41,866 --> 00:20:42,949
Send it back.

327
00:20:43,868 --> 00:20:44,701
No, wait.

328
00:20:45,787 --> 00:20:47,621
(somber music)

329
00:20:47,622 --> 00:20:51,792
How 'bout, uh, what about
to Anderson, Montgomery,

330
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:54,878
Berkley, Pincus,

331
00:20:58,424 --> 00:20:59,883
Gianelli, Winters?

332
00:21:03,304 --> 00:21:06,181
(bottle thudding)

333
00:21:06,182 --> 00:21:08,725
(somber music continues)

334
00:21:08,726 --> 00:21:13,730
(computer beeping)
(dramatic music)

335
00:21:21,322 --> 00:21:22,489
(fingers tapping)

336
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:25,409
(computer beeping)

337
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:39,464
(door clattering)

338
00:21:40,842 --> 00:21:41,925
How's Loomis?

339
00:21:42,802 --> 00:21:44,761
Uh, he's gonna need a little surgery,

340
00:21:44,762 --> 00:21:46,680
but, uh, he'll be okay.

341
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,434
What's up?

342
00:21:50,435 --> 00:21:53,019
Special ops, (laughs) they want a word.

343
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:53,854
Aw, forget it.

344
00:21:53,855 --> 00:21:55,272
I don't have the time.

345
00:21:55,273 --> 00:21:57,357
Better make time, Sean.

346
00:21:58,234 --> 00:22:00,569
Recovered from the jet wreckage.

347
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:03,029
Found in Pollux Troy's briefcase.

348
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:06,491
(suspenseful music)

349
00:22:06,492 --> 00:22:10,162
(disk clattering)

350
00:22:10,163 --> 00:22:15,167
(sultry music)
(woman moaning)

351
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:24,176
Porcelain casing, thermal cloak,

352
00:22:25,261 --> 00:22:28,430
nerve gas, and biological payload.

353
00:22:28,431 --> 00:22:30,724
It's enough to flatten a square mile.

354
00:22:30,725 --> 00:22:33,477
Then, depending on the prevailing winds,

355
00:22:33,478 --> 00:22:37,898
the fallout'll be a tad
worse than Gulf War syndrome.

356
00:22:40,234 --> 00:22:42,694
A biblical, a biblical plague to LA.

357
00:22:42,695 --> 00:22:44,654
Fuck. (screams)
(hand thudding)

358
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:46,156
Where is he?

359
00:22:46,157 --> 00:22:47,908
Where is Pollux Troy?

360
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:50,327
(pensive music)

361
00:22:50,328 --> 00:22:51,411
(paper thudding)

362
00:22:51,412 --> 00:22:52,537
Why draw the schematic

363
00:22:52,538 --> 00:22:55,165
if you're not gonna build the bomb, hmm?

364
00:22:55,166 --> 00:22:56,666
- [Pollux] What, is it now
a crime in this country

365
00:22:56,667 --> 00:22:58,251
to exercise the mind?

366
00:22:58,252 --> 00:22:59,961
- I'm interested in bomb-
- I won't say another word

367
00:22:59,962 --> 00:23:01,880
until I see my brother.

368
00:23:04,467 --> 00:23:06,551
Any progress?

369
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:08,345
- I need about 10 minutes
alone with this guy.

370
00:23:08,346 --> 00:23:09,471
Ah, give it a rest.

371
00:23:09,472 --> 00:23:10,305
You got Castor.

372
00:23:10,306 --> 00:23:11,139
Just go home.

373
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:11,973
(Sean sighing)

374
00:23:11,974 --> 00:23:14,267
Look, we're not gonna evacuate
the city on your hunch.

375
00:23:14,268 --> 00:23:17,521
- Look, I know Castor too
well for this to be a hunch.

376
00:23:17,522 --> 00:23:18,313
You know what?

377
00:23:18,314 --> 00:23:22,067
Just, just run the goddamn
Bureau any way ya like.

378
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:23,902
(dramatic music)

379
00:23:23,903 --> 00:23:27,030
(door slamming)

380
00:23:27,031 --> 00:23:29,616
(Sean sighing)

381
00:23:31,244 --> 00:23:33,912
I could put an agent in his cell.

382
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:35,372
Maybe Pollux will let it slip.

383
00:23:35,373 --> 00:23:36,665
Oh, come on.

384
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:39,084
He's a paranoid sociopath.

385
00:23:39,085 --> 00:23:41,878
The only person he'd talk to
about that bomb is his brother,

386
00:23:41,879 --> 00:23:43,046
and he's dead.

387
00:23:44,173 --> 00:23:46,716
There is one other possibility.

388
00:23:46,717 --> 00:23:49,719
(suspenseful music)

389
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:58,478
(door buzzing and clattering)

390
00:24:12,368 --> 00:24:15,787
Oh, God, you're keeping him alive.

391
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:17,581
Relax, Archer.

392
00:24:17,582 --> 00:24:18,415
He's a turnip.

393
00:24:18,416 --> 00:24:21,501
(cigarette hissing)

394
00:24:21,502 --> 00:24:22,377
Oh.

395
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:27,257
- What if you could
walk into Erewhon Prison

396
00:24:27,258 --> 00:24:32,095
and give Pollux a nice, big,
brotherly hug as Castor Troy?

397
00:24:33,139 --> 00:24:35,557
- I have no idea what
you're talking about.

398
00:24:35,558 --> 00:24:37,267
Let me try.

399
00:24:37,268 --> 00:24:38,977
Malcolm Walsh.

400
00:24:38,978 --> 00:24:40,812
I run the bio-cover unit for special ops.

401
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:41,771
I know who you are.

402
00:24:41,772 --> 00:24:43,982
But you don't know what I can do.

403
00:24:43,983 --> 00:24:45,609
- Uh-
- Physical alteration.

404
00:24:45,610 --> 00:24:47,360
Augmentation.

405
00:24:47,403 --> 00:24:49,279
- [Hollis] Dr. Walsh
can alter the likeness,

406
00:24:49,322 --> 00:24:51,698
even the voice of a government witness.

407
00:24:51,699 --> 00:24:54,159
I think you'll recognize this patient.

408
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:58,163
(suspenseful music continues)

409
00:24:58,164 --> 00:24:59,497
We had to build your friend Loomis

410
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:01,666
a whole new ear from scratch.
(fingers tapping)

411
00:25:01,667 --> 00:25:04,419
(lasers buzzing)

412
00:25:10,676 --> 00:25:12,344
What we're suggesting for you, Archer,

413
00:25:12,345 --> 00:25:14,638
isn't a permanent transplant like that,

414
00:25:14,639 --> 00:25:16,556
just a temporary trade.

415
00:25:17,725 --> 00:25:18,558
Come here.

416
00:25:20,603 --> 00:25:22,354
(fingers tapping)

417
00:25:22,355 --> 00:25:23,647
With the new anti-inflammatories,

418
00:25:23,648 --> 00:25:26,316
healing takes days, not weeks.

419
00:25:26,317 --> 00:25:28,693
Your blood types won't match,
but Pollux won't know that.

420
00:25:28,694 --> 00:25:31,321
Height difference is negligible.

421
00:25:33,574 --> 00:25:38,453
Skin pigment, eye pigment,
both almost identical.

422
00:25:38,454 --> 00:25:41,122
We'll use laser shears for the hairline,

423
00:25:41,123 --> 00:25:43,458
microplugs for body hair.

424
00:25:43,459 --> 00:25:44,793
We'll do an abdominoplasty,

425
00:25:44,794 --> 00:25:47,879
take care of those, uh, love handles.

426
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:50,423
But all that's the easy part.
(laser buzzing)

427
00:25:50,424 --> 00:25:52,717
Here's the real science.

428
00:25:52,718 --> 00:25:56,262
This is a state-of-the-art
morphogenetic template.

429
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:59,516
The inside is modeled on your skull,

430
00:25:59,517 --> 00:26:02,060
the outside exactly like Troy's.

431
00:26:02,061 --> 00:26:04,187
Then, we fit his face on top,

432
00:26:04,188 --> 00:26:06,106
not a replica, but the real thing.

433
00:26:06,107 --> 00:26:07,565
Then, we simply connect the muscles,

434
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,900
tear ducts, and nerve endings.

435
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:10,735
So, you wanna take his face and mine-

436
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:12,153
Borrow.

437
00:26:12,154 --> 00:26:14,739
The procedure's completely reversible.

438
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:17,742
- You, you think that I
want to do this? (laughs)

439
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:19,995
No, no.
- There's no one else, Sean.

440
00:26:19,996 --> 00:26:20,870
No.

441
00:26:20,871 --> 00:26:23,498
- You have lived and breathed
Castor Troy for years.

442
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:24,916
I'll get his gang to talk.

443
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:26,960
That's what I do.
- What if you can't?

444
00:26:26,961 --> 00:26:30,714
The bomb will blow, and
Castor Troy will win.

445
00:26:32,967 --> 00:26:33,883
(body thudding)
(items clattering)

446
00:26:33,884 --> 00:26:34,843
Get out.

447
00:26:34,844 --> 00:26:36,177
Go ahead.

448
00:26:36,178 --> 00:26:37,345
Wipe your ass.

449
00:26:37,346 --> 00:26:39,514
Damn, what the hell is that smell?

450
00:26:39,515 --> 00:26:40,348
He shit in his pants.

451
00:26:40,349 --> 00:26:41,474
Where's Dietrich?

452
00:26:41,475 --> 00:26:43,309
(chair rasping)

453
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:45,854
Hello, Sasha. (sighs)

454
00:26:45,855 --> 00:26:48,314
When was the last time
you saw Castor Troy?

455
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:49,357
Who cares? He's dead.

456
00:26:49,358 --> 00:26:50,608
Answer the question.

457
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:52,027
I know my rights.

458
00:26:52,028 --> 00:26:53,361
I don't have to answer shit.

459
00:26:53,362 --> 00:26:55,447
You're right, but know this.

460
00:26:55,448 --> 00:26:57,574
You're a convicted felon on probation

461
00:26:57,575 --> 00:26:59,159
for harboring Castor Troy.
(suspenseful music)

462
00:26:59,160 --> 00:27:00,326
One phone call from me,

463
00:27:00,327 --> 00:27:03,830
and your son will end up in a foster home.

464
00:27:05,458 --> 00:27:07,208
(Sasha sighs)

465
00:27:07,209 --> 00:27:11,129
- I understand why you
would use such a threat.

466
00:27:11,130 --> 00:27:15,550
But you try to take him away
from me, I swear to you.

467
00:27:19,096 --> 00:27:21,514
I haven't seen him for years.

468
00:27:25,519 --> 00:27:26,478
(hand thudding)

469
00:27:26,479 --> 00:27:29,397
(switch clicking)

470
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:32,942
(lighter clicking)

471
00:27:32,943 --> 00:27:35,779
(door clattering)

472
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,198
This reeks of you.

473
00:27:38,199 --> 00:27:41,201
It's got your signature all over it.

474
00:27:42,411 --> 00:27:46,915
- Maybe, but you ain't got
nothing on me, and you know it.

475
00:27:46,916 --> 00:27:51,086
- Maybe so, but I can keep
you within city limits,

476
00:27:51,087 --> 00:27:53,213
or I can talk to your sister again.

477
00:27:53,214 --> 00:27:54,839
She's right outside.

478
00:27:56,258 --> 00:27:58,676
Only this time, I'll be nice.

479
00:28:00,179 --> 00:28:01,179
Hey, Sean.

480
00:28:02,848 --> 00:28:04,516
How's your dead son?

481
00:28:06,560 --> 00:28:09,395
(Dietrich laughing)

482
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:10,355
(body thudding)

483
00:28:10,356 --> 00:28:13,441
(gun clanking)
(dramatic music)

484
00:28:13,442 --> 00:28:14,734
I don't know anything.

485
00:28:14,735 --> 00:28:16,736
Okay, okay, I heard
something about the 18th,

486
00:28:16,737 --> 00:28:18,613
but that's all I know.

487
00:28:19,907 --> 00:28:21,074
(gun clanking)

488
00:28:21,075 --> 00:28:23,034
(door clattering)

489
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:25,620
(Sean sighing)

490
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,958
Great, so we got a date.

491
00:28:29,959 --> 00:28:31,459
Now, where the hell's the damn bomb?

492
00:28:31,460 --> 00:28:33,628
Only Pollux Troy'll know that.

493
00:28:33,629 --> 00:28:36,089
It's your call, Sean.

494
00:28:36,090 --> 00:28:37,841
Does Lazarro know your plan?

495
00:28:37,842 --> 00:28:40,343
No, this is a black-bag operation,

496
00:28:40,344 --> 00:28:42,137
strictly off the books.

497
00:28:42,138 --> 00:28:45,265
You can't tell Lazarro, and
you can't tell your wife.

498
00:28:45,266 --> 00:28:47,976
(suspenseful music)

499
00:28:47,977 --> 00:28:48,768
Oh, God.

500
00:28:50,187 --> 00:28:51,563
What are you asking me to do?

501
00:28:51,564 --> 00:28:52,897
Okay, let's see.

502
00:28:53,858 --> 00:28:58,194
You're asking me to, to
break the law, risk my neck.

503
00:29:00,489 --> 00:29:03,616
And you're asking me to put
in the dark all the people

504
00:29:03,617 --> 00:29:05,785
that love me and trust me.

505
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:11,541
(suspenseful music continues)

506
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:17,297
(Sean sighing)

507
00:29:17,298 --> 00:29:18,214
I'll do it.

508
00:29:22,553 --> 00:29:25,305
(door clattering)
(engine humming)

509
00:29:25,306 --> 00:29:27,891
(dog barking)

510
00:29:35,983 --> 00:29:38,735
(latch clicking)

511
00:29:47,369 --> 00:29:50,288
(bedding rustling)

512
00:29:57,671 --> 00:29:58,588
Mm, Sean.

513
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:04,802
Sorry I woke you.

514
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:08,723
- No, I'm glad it's you
that woke me (laughs)

515
00:30:08,724 --> 00:30:13,186
and not a phone call telling
me you won't be coming home.

516
00:30:13,187 --> 00:30:17,023
But that's a fear I can
finally let go of, huh?

517
00:30:17,024 --> 00:30:19,651
(lips smacking)

518
00:30:24,490 --> 00:30:26,658
(Eve exhaling)

519
00:30:26,659 --> 00:30:28,326
Oh, it's all right, Sean.

520
00:30:28,327 --> 00:30:29,160
It's okay.

521
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:33,289
I keep,

522
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:38,836
I keep wanting to move
this over here, you know?

523
00:30:40,714 --> 00:30:44,384
If it had only been an,
an inch to the left,

524
00:30:45,469 --> 00:30:46,886
Mikey'd be alive.

525
00:30:48,097 --> 00:30:49,889
And you wouldn't be.

526
00:30:52,726 --> 00:30:56,062
Sean, things are gonna get
better now that you're home.

527
00:30:56,063 --> 00:31:00,275
The scar won't move, but
it will heal if you let it.

528
00:31:00,276 --> 00:31:01,192
Everything will be better now

529
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:04,112
that he's forever out of our lives.

530
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:09,534
(Sean sighing)

531
00:31:09,535 --> 00:31:12,120
(gentle music)

532
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,916
Eve, if I told you that I realized

